  "prefLabel": "Gcd 214.04 Issuance of Declaratory Rulings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Gcd 214.04 Issuance of Declaratory Rulings. When facts sufficient to support a declaratory ruling or to justify denial of a declaratory ruling have been established, the commission shall:\n\n(a) Issue a written declaratory ruling which applies all relevant law to the established facts; or\n\n(b) Issue a written decision that the commission lacks the subject matter or personal jurisdiction required for the issuance of a declaratory ruling.\n\nSource. #7635-A, eff 1-30-02; ss by #10339, eff 5-17-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/gcd100-400.html"
}
